  "note": [
    "Path -> category mapping for the release governance-vs-product measurement.",
    "Versioned so a later reading is comparable to an earlier one: a reading records",
    "the taxonomy_version it was computed under, and a bump means prior readings are",
    "recomputed rather than silently compared across two different rulers.",
    "Matching is LONGEST-PREFIX-WINS over the repository-relative path. A path that",
    "matches no rule is reported as `unclassified` -- a first-class state, never a",
    "silent default. `unclassified` alone does not make a commit `mixed`.",
    "The `consumer` label names a SHIPPED SURFACE, not delivered consumer value.",
    "openai/codex-default asked for the label `shipped-product` on exactly that",
    "ground and anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5 preferred keeping `consumer` for",
    "consistency with the roadmap's own wording; the roadmap's wording is kept and",
    "the objection is recorded here rather than dropped."
  ],
  "categories": {
    "consumer": "Shipped surface an installing consumer receives or invokes: skills, rules, commands, guidelines, packs, the agent-config CLI runtime, and user-facing documentation.",
    "governance": "This repository's own steering layer: roadmaps, evidence ledgers, verdicts, decision records, archive and promotion records, and governance-only contracts.",
    "maintenance": "Repository infrastructure: CI gates, tests, build and release automation, packaging, dependencies, tooling configuration.",
    "unclassified": "No rule matches, or the path is genuinely shared between categories and is left visible rather than assigned."
  },
  "excluded_generated": [
    "dist/",
    ".augment/",
    ".claude/",
    ".cursor/",
    ".clinerules/",
    ".windsurfrules",
    "GEMINI.md",
    ".claude-plugin/",
    ".augment-plugin/",
    "package-lock.json",
    "docs/decisions/INDEX.md",
    "agents/roadmaps/archive/INDEX.md",
    "agents/roadmaps/archive/index.json"
  ],
  "excluded_note": [
    "Generated projections and lockfiles are removed BEFORE a commit is classified,",
    "and are excluded from both the commit view and the diff view. A commit left with",
    "no path after the exclusion is counted in the `generated_only` diagnostic rather",
    "than as maintenance -- otherwise a release's ratio would depend on whether the",
    "regeneration was committed separately from the source edit that caused it."
  ],
